    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-7196",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c514865c-02d0-5d59-938b-fdd739cdb257",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Velocity Vector Given the Acceleration Vector",
      "problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na=⟨1,2⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨4,3⟩$ when $t=1$, calculate the velocity vector of $P$ at time $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨1,2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t+{C}_{1},2t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨4,3⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨1+{C}_{1},2(1)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨4,3⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},2+{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =1+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =2+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv=⟨t+3,2t+1⟩.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
